Make jaccard estimation multithreaded
Put everything in the hdf5 file: no need for a directory.

Create a generic interface for kmer counting that returns the kmers/counts
Move all intersection/filtering logic to this generic class
Get a proper hash function and rename xxhash stuff (we're not actually using that)
Set a memory limit on loaded sketches during jaccard calculation, then load two blocks at a time with half that memory.
    Keeping a left and right block and swapping them when we move between block rows will reduce loading times.
Remove remainder of C/cython code: use C++/pybind11 only.
Work out if it's possible to move to C++11.
